    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'd say he clearly knew this hill was steep. The meetings he's had over the course of the last couple of days with Republican senators, as he's gained it out, that there's not a path to victory. And if there's not a path to confirmation, why go through it? Because it does become a distraction. And not just to him, but to the Senate, to the president, I would say whatever the circumstances are, this is one of the more positive things Matt Gates has done in a while. And I think in terms of his patriotism, in terms of his honor, in terms of his respect for the institutions, good for him to recognize that early on and prevent further wasting of resources.",
