    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "my advice actually to Matt, I have not talked to him. He called me a few days ago. I called him back. He left a voicemail. I called him back. His voicemail hadn't been set up. Um, I talked to President Trump about it. Um, Sunday on the phone, uh, I was on the plane with him as I said Tuesday. We did not talk about it on Tuesday other than just him expressing. I do. I wish we could get this cross finish line. But I've been very open about it. I mean, I've been everywhere about it on every network pretty much. Just saying that the Hill is very, very steep and the capital that you'd have to spend to succeed, much less probably not succeed with the confirmation would be probably more than it would be worth. And I think that's how he gained it out and good for him for not, like I said, not spending a lot more capital. Political capital is our currency. Political capital is what you gather by doing things for people, with your partners, with your colleagues, and then it's to be spent on them doing things for you. It's a transactional business, and a lot of people find that offensive to which I say, gee, talk to the founders of our great country.",
