    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "is different. It is. It's a different standard. But yeah, so he has struggled and granted that we have two of those years of 50-50 Senate and the other one, 51-49, which is both the same thing when you have the Vice President. And he's come up short a few times. So it's not the worst thing to happen for a president whose party is empowering the Senate because I think it actually speaks to how damn smart our founders were when they created this whole system. of a check and a balance of advice and consent by the Senate to make sure that we don't have a king, but that we have these three co-equal branches. It's kind of a wonderful, I think, description of it. And when, you know, I take a little heat, I do a lot of talk radio a couple hours a week in North Dakota. I did two shows already this morning. And when people push on me a little bit on it, and like one did last night, I just say, I want you to imagine the tables being turned and Joe Biden being the president and the Democrats being in control, would you ever suggest that my loyalty, that their loyalty, where would you be critical if a Democrat senator's loyalty was to Joe Biden and not to the Constitution and conscience? And that's the whole point of the system of ours is that there is a second balance. So I think it's pretty good evidence that our system works.",
