        "text": "The Founders designed the U.S. government with a system of checks and balances to prevent monarchy.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "There have been two years with a 50-50 split in the Senate and one year with a 51-49 split.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The Vice President breaks ties in the Senate, making 50-50 and 51-49 outcomes functionally equivalent.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The Senate’s role includes providing advice and consent, ensuring co-equality among branches.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The current political situation involves a different standard than previous ones.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The president has failed to achieve certain legislative goals despite his party controlling the Senate.",
