    "turn_text": "No, I think you're going to see what you'd normally see. Now, I will say Donald Trump is non-conventional, and he is pointing, nominating a lot of non-conventional people. But I do think what's different this go around a couple of things. One is he has the experience of the benefit of four years, and of four years that had a slow start to it. a bureaucracy that he thought was going to be more compliant than they turned out to be. And so he's never going to make that mistake again. The second thing is he doesn't get another term after this. So he's got a sense of urgency about it that's real. We all have that same thing. We know how precious and how unusual, really, these moments are when we have a president and a Senate, pretty good, 53, 47 majority Senate of the same party. And none of us wants to be responsible for screwing it up. And so, for the most part, we're going to yield to him as long as it's...",
