    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95952.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 60,
    "turn_text": "It is because, listen, I'm grateful for every airman and soldier, and guardian, and marine, and sailor, and Coast Guardsman that puts on uniform and defends us, for sure. But in the case of Lloyd Austin, that didn't seem to help him as a Secretary of Defense. But I also realize he works for a Commander-in-Chief who's not really very qualified. When you use the word qualifications in these appointed and elected positions, the thing we have to remember is the only qualification required is that he has the confidence of the president and can get enough votes to be confirmed. That's our political system. I have two really favorite paintings. And the rotunda, one of them is that one of the pilgrims, the demarcation of the pilgrims. And the other one is George Washington, surrendering his credentials as a military commission, his commission as a military general. Because in our system, generals don't run the country. Civilians are the leaders of our military. And that's by design on purpose. And so I think Pete, in terms of his service, We'll bring something that we haven't had in a long time, and that is not a general, a general-turn secretary, which I remember we had to change the rules. We had to waive the rules, both for Mattis and for Austin, to even be the secretary, because our rules require a longer period between service and political service. I think Pete brings that warrior's heart. I think that the warriors out there, they always have. He's very popular with veterans, enlisted veterans especially. And remembering that this very large organization isn't run by one person. It's not run by the Commander Chief. It's not run by the Secretary. It's not run by the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff. It's run by a whole bunch of talented people",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
