    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "For sure, image matters, obviously. But at the same time, if we allow allegations to set the bar, then everybody, no matter who they are, runs the risk of not being qualified because of an allegation. So we have to be fairer both to the victims and to the alleged perpetrators. And that's all. I just think our system has to do that. We've had issues. We've had some very detailed issues that we've addressed with general officers with false allegations as well as proven allegations. And we have to deal with them, I think, based on the evidence that comes out. But in the case of Secretary, again, this is the president's decision as to whether he's, if there are other factors that are important to him and he weighs all of that. And I think what we have to do the same thing, but it will require us a hearing. It will require background checks. It will require these personal meetings that he's having with senators, and it will require at least 50 senators to go along.",
