    "turn_text": "Well, I would rather that we give him the resources, the law enforcement resources to do that. It's a better use of law enforcement. And it's not a great use of the military. I mean, our military has pretty, we have pretty specific policies about policing, for example, our military can be helpful in lots of ways that could be helpful You know, even in the deportation process, but what they don't have is policing powers. They don't have arrest authorities, for example, authorization, for example, you know, force authorization, anything like that. And I think that's important to maintain. I personally think that the deportation is going to be better and easier than a lot of people think it is, partly because even the draw of illegal immigration is based largely on the attitude of the country and the policies of welcoming. I mean, why had 10 to 20 million people come here illegally when Joe Biden was president because he said they should?",
