    "turn_text": "appropriation package. It could be part of a budget reconciliation package where we up that budget. I see. And, you know, he's gonna meet resistance from, from, um, sanctuaries, sanctuary cities. Police departments and whatnot because the mayors are going to tell them don't cooperate with those guys. That's why we're a sanctuary and all of that. To the degree that he can influence that, I think we can do that through finance, through the budget. Why we would allow a city in the United States of America to say we will not cooperate with the federal government's policies on illegal immigration and criminal illegal immigration. and we still send the money for policing, you know, that this makes no sense. So I do think we need to look at our federal policies and if there are cities that want to be sanctuaries for criminals, then they shouldn't get money for policing. In fact, one of the things that killed the bipartisan bill that there's got so much attention in the campaign was that there was extra money additional money for sanctuary cities. I mean the idea we would reward a city for being a sanctuary for criminals as long as they're here illegally is the most absurd policy yet and there's a lot of absurd policies.",
