    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95952.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 140,
    "turn_text": "using the military wrong people up. Where I've been the most outspoken and I have talked to people on transition about this. the idea that we would form a commission to go after general officers who are, quote, woke, or because they pushed the DEI agenda too far. It's similar to the withdrawal in one sense, but in a broader sense, it's much worse because During the Biden administration's first couple of years, the Deputy Secretary, for example, of the Air Force was Gina Ortiz. Secretary Ortiz required all of the commanders and the generals to read the DEI statement and to make sure the troops read or heard their DEI statement, and they resisted that and she pushed them out. I don't think we should become the police on the other side of this. I think, again, this is evidence that general officers and everybody that wears uniforms, salutes to the political leadership. That's our system, we like that system. I don't think, I think it sends a bad message to the troops, if there's gonna be a commission that goes after them, if something goes wrong, or if a political leader makes a dumb decision. I want young men and women who are considering military service, or who are in military service, or young officers. I want them to look at somebody like a CQ Brown. If you're a young black man that's aspires to be great, I want you to look at CQ Braggle. I want to be like that guy.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
