  {
    "episode_id": 95952,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95952.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 160,
    "turn_text": "I want to talk just briefly about some of the people who are going to play key roles in this relationship between Senate Republicans and the White House. One is JD Vance on the chamber floor last night during votes very late at night. He was up here with Gates and Hex up this week. But I'll be honest with you, my impression, at least before he became VP, you know, Trump's running me, was that there were a number of Senate Republicans who didn't actually like him. I'm curious if you can tell us about his relationship with some folks up here. And like, has he tried to improve? Like he's, he's number one, he's new. But number two, I think some people sort of have viewed him as a bomb thrower in an institution that, you know, frankly, prefers pragmatism. Very deliberate.",
