    "turn_text": "JD is a great voice and face for the populist movement, generational change, certainly in the White House and within the United States Senate. So what I think is a little different in JD's role is that because Donald Trump himself has so many personal relationships, JD can, you know, he'll have the most influence over like-minded senators, and there are a lot of them. I mean, there's JD represents granted in a much more eloquent and intellectual way than perhaps some others, but represents a significant part of the conservative population as do a whole bunch of senators. I think JD helped Donald Trump win, and I think he'll help him on the hill. Not everybody has the same regard for JD. I don't know how you can't like him, though. I would say this. If anybody wants to not like JD Vath, you better never meet him. He is truly a genuine, sincere, eloquent, intellectual conscience of the populist movement. That's what I've told him a couple of times.",
